{
  "_comment": [
    "Hand-written two-storey demo (schema_version 2): the acceptance scene for the",
    "multi-floor contract.  Ground floor: hall (with the switchback stair), living,",
    "kitchen, dining; upper floor: landing, bedroom, study, bath above the same",
    "footprint.  One switchback stair (16 risers, half landing) connects hall ->",
    "landing through a slab opening; the two floors share their walls in XY, so the",
    "same door positions on both storeys prove the per-storey cutters.",
    "z of furniture and cameras is a WORLD height: the upper floor walking surface",
    "is at 2.85 m (2.7 m storey + 0.15 m slab), so upper cameras sit at 4.35 m and",
    "the tables/lamps quote their world heights.  window sill/height stay relative",
    "to the room floor.  See blender_agent/spec.py for the frozen contract."
  ],
